# Built try-on engine (generated by `npm run build:engine` from repo root).
#
# COMMITTED, not built on deploy. The theme block iframes /tryon/index.html, so
# this must exist in production. Building it on Vercel proved too fragile: the
# engine build lives at the monorepo root, but Vercel's Root Directory is
# apps/shopify-app and its cached/partial install did not reliably provide the
# root build tooling -- three separate deploys failed (basic-ssl pruned, then
# three unresolved from the temp config, then a stale build cache; see git log
# ~2026-07-25). So we commit the TRIMMED engine and Vercel serves it statically
# via react-router build copying public/ into build/client/.
#
# Regenerate with `npm run build:engine` from the repo root, then strip the
# dev-only and authoring assets before committing (the ignore rules below keep
# them out automatically): mock-turn/, mock-face.png, harness/, and every model
# except the runtime *-draco.glb files the SKU catalog references.
/public/tryon/mock-turn/
/public/tryon/mock-face.png
/public/tryon/harness/
/public/tryon/models/*
!/public/tryon/models/*-draco.glb
# gripzpelmo demo loads the RAW model (useNormalizedModel:false), so the raw
# GLB must ship too — otherwise /tryon/models/gripzpelmo.glb 404s in production.
!/public/tryon/models/gripzpelmo.glb
/prisma/dev.sqlite
/prisma/dev.sqlite-journal
database.sqlite

# Legacy dev-slice local model storage. Production stores calibrated GLBs in R2
# (app/storage.server.js); nothing writes here anymore.
/storage/

.env
.env.*
# ...but the committed template carries no secrets and must stay tracked.
!.env.example





/extensions/*/dist

# Ignore shopify files created during app dev
.shopify/*
.shopify.lock

# Hide files auto-generated by react router
.react-router/

# Vercel build output + local link metadata
.vercel/